# ===========================================================================
# WHAT NEVER ENTERS THIS REPOSITORY'S HISTORY.
#
# REWRITTEN 5 Sep 2026, AFTER THE FRESH `init`. The repository is built from
# PUBLIC-REPO-TAKE-LIST.txt — nothing ships unless it is named there — and
# PUBLIC-REPO-CONFIG.json's `ignore` list is where every deliberate
# leave-behind is written down, one rule at a time, with the preview printing
# a count of what each rule swallowed. THAT LIST IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH AND
# THIS FILE IS BROUGHT INTO AGREEMENT WITH IT.
#
# ── THE TWO FILES ANSWER DIFFERENT QUESTIONS, WHICH IS WHY BOTH EXIST ──────
#
# PUBLIC-REPO-CONFIG.json asks: WHAT MAY THE TAKE LIST LEAVE BEHIND WITHOUT A
# DECISION? Anything in this folder that is neither on the take list nor
# matched by a rule there is a REFUSAL — a thing somebody must classify. Its
# rules exist to be counted.
#
# THIS FILE ASKS: WHAT MUST NEVER REACH THE INDEX FROM THIS WORKING FOLDER ON
# THIS MACHINE? That is a superset. It carries editor droppings, local logs
# and scratch names that do not exist in a clone and that the config has no
# reason to name — and it carries them because the cost of a stray file here
# is a commit, not a printed line.
#
# SO: EVERY CONFIG RULE APPEARS HERE. THIS FILE ADDS A FEW AND THE ADDITIONS
# ARE MARKED. Where a config rule is a bare directory name it is written here
# with a trailing `/` so it cannot also swallow a file of that name.
#
# ── WHAT THIS FILE DOES NOT DO ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# IGNORING A TRACKED FILE DOES NOTHING. TEN files are in the first commit and
# should not be — seven documents that should never have shipped, and three
# scripts taken off the take list afterwards. The rules for all ten are below
# AND the removal is UNTRACK-SHIPPED-BY-MISTAKE.command, which is a separate
# act by a person.
# Every other process file in this folder was never tracked at all — the
# fresh `init` honoured a take list that does not name them — and that is
# a property of THE REPOSITORY CREATED ON 5 Sep, not of the one before it.
# ===========================================================================


# ── EDITOR, OS AND MACHINE DROPPINGS ───────────────────────────────────────
# `**/.DS_Store` is in the config and is redundant here: a gitignore pattern
# with no slash already matches at every depth.
.DS_Store
.fuse_hidden*
# NOT IN THE CONFIG, AND DELIBERATE. A clone has no stray logs and no local
# notes, so the config never has to name them; this folder does.
*.log
NOTES.md
scratch/


# ── BUILD OUTPUT AND INSTALLED DEPENDENCIES ────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
.data/

# Compact build output. Regenerate with `npm run compact`.
contracts/managed/
contracts/managed-vault/
# The symlink `compile-vault.sh` makes so the vault's generated caller can find
# the account's generated module at the path it imports. Build output pointing
# at build output.
contracts/Acct
contracts/build/

# PROBE OUTPUT — THROWAWAY COMPILER RUNS CARRYING PROVING AND VERIFIER KEYS
# MEASURED IN MEGABYTES.
#
# THESE FOUR RULES USED TO NAME `contracts/probe/`, `contracts/probe4/` and
# `contracts/probe5/`, WHICH DO NOT EXIST UNDER THOSE NAMES, AND MATCHED NONE
# OF THE FOUR DIRECTORIES THAT DO. What exists and was matched by nothing:
# contracts/chainprobe/ (42 M), contracts/probe-unshielded/ (5.1 M),
# contracts/probe-branch/, contracts/probe-k/. The rule written to stop probe
# output entering history did not match the probe output on this disk.
#
# The take list is the real control — nothing ships unless it is named — and
# these rules are the second line, so they now match directories that exist
# rather than directories somebody remembered.
contracts/probe*/
contracts/chainprobe/


# ── NETWORK STATE, KEYS AND SECRETS ────────────────────────────────────────
# THE WALLET SEED THAT HOLDS THIS PROJECT'S FUNDS IS IN HERE, IN PLAIN TEXT.
# Losing it means asking the faucet again; committing it means anyone who
# reads the repository can spend those funds. The door that refuses a tree
# containing any value read out of these files is scripts/secret-scan.mjs,
# and it runs inside COMMIT.command — because a key in a published history
# cannot be taken back by any later edit.
.midnight/
.env
.env.example
.keys-backup/
.wallet-state/
# The private state store: contract-address-keyed, rebuilt on demand, and it
# holds signer secrets in an encrypted LevelDB.
midnight-level-db/
# NOT IN THE CONFIG. A local convenience file that has never existed here and
# would carry the same values as `.env` if it did.
.env.local

# `.env.example` IS IGNORED ON A RULING AND NOT BY OVERSIGHT. It is the one
# file the scanner structurally cannot clear: it is BOTH a secret root and a
# candidate to ship, and a value is never searched for inside the file it was
# read out of — so the door reported it SUPPRESSED, `nothing below is a
# refusal and nothing below has been checked`, rather than passing it. Ruled
# 5 Sep: env files can be added incrementally later. Leave it out.


# ── EVERYTHING THE `.command` FILES LEAVE BEHIND ───────────────────────────
# Reports, stack samples and symbol maps. `REPORT-*.txt` does not match the
# bare `REPORT.txt`, so that one is named.
REPORT-*.txt
REPORT.txt
logs/

# Scratch left behind where `rm` is unavailable, and pre-reset archives. Both
# are cleared out by hand. The config names one dated archive; the glob here
# is wider on purpose — the next one will have a different date.
_to_delete/
.pre-reset-*/
.s38-scratch/


# ── CLONED SOURCE THAT BELONGS TO SOMEBODY ELSE ────────────────────────────
# The Foundation's source and SAFE's, cloned in so this folder is
# self-contained and a scope can cite source rather than memory.
midnight-src/
/SAFE/

# Identity is its own repository. Nothing under here belongs to this one.
/Identity/


# ── THE THREE FILES A COMMIT IS BUILT FROM, WHICH A COMMIT MUST NOT CARRY ──
# What it says, what it contains, where it goes. Each is rewritten whole for
# every commit, so tracking one would put the last commit's version inside the
# next commit — the message about the message.
COMMIT-MESSAGE.md
COMMIT-FILES.txt
COMMIT-BRANCH.txt
# The record PUBLIC-REPO-APPLY.command writes when it has run. It describes one
# machine at one moment, like a report.
PUBLIC-REPO-APPLIED.txt


# ── THE MIGRATION'S OWN TOOLING AND ITS TWO LISTS ──────────────────────────
# The config describes this process, and the take list is a decision record
# with our own reasoning in it. Neither is software.
PUBLIC-REPO-CONFIG.json
PUBLIC-REPO-TAKE-LIST.txt
scripts/public-repo.mjs
scripts/public-repo.test.ts


# ── THE `.command` FILES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# v1 ships none of them. They stay in this folder exactly where they are and
# keep working; they are simply never committed.
#
# THE COST IS REAL AND IT IS WRITTEN DOWN RATHER THAN DISCOVERED: 116 small
# contract programs and 130 deliberate breakages live inside those files and
# nowhere else in this folder. Moving that work into `scripts/` is its own
# round. If it does not happen, this rule is where the loss began.
*.command


# ── TWO TRACKED-LOOKING SCRIPTS THAT OPEN PRIVATE DOCUMENTS AT RUN TIME ────
# Both would ship a permanently broken tool AND publish the shape of the
# private process.
# check-backlog-ids.py opens BACKLOG.md; check-board-integrity.mjs opens the
# board and the register. A trailing comment is not a comment in this file —
# gitignore reads the whole line as the pattern — so they go above.
scripts/check-backlog-ids.py
scripts/check-board-integrity.mjs


# ── THREE SCRIPTS TAKEN OFF THE TAKE LIST 5 Sep ────────────────────────────
# The two probes are a research RECORD, not a tool, and both hard-code one
# machine's browser binary, so neither runs in a clone. `new-wallet.ts` is
# referenced by nothing anywhere and writes `.midnight/wallet.seed`. All three
# stay on disk.
#
# **AND ALL THREE ARE ALREADY IN THE INDEX**, so these rules do not remove
# them — nothing about ignoring a tracked file does. They come out with the
# seven below, in UNTRACK-SHIPPED-BY-MISTAKE.command, which names all ten.
scripts/prf-probe.mjs
scripts/prf-probe-failure-mode.mjs
scripts/new-wallet.ts


# ── WORKING DOCUMENTS AT THE ROOT ──────────────────────────────────────────
# AUDIT-FABLE.md's own line 3 says it is gitignored; until this rewrite it was
# not. HANDOVER.md says "Not on GitHub" inside itself. XXkUxM9m is zero bytes
# with a random name, referenced by nothing.
AUDIT-FABLE.md
BACKLOG.md
CLAUDE.md
HANDOVER.md
KICKOFF.md
UPSTREAM-DUST-WALLET.md
pi4a-cut.mjs
/XXkUxM9m


# ── docs/ — THE DESIGN SET SHIPS AND NOTHING ELSE DOES ─────────────────────
# The round documents, the board, the build order, the backlog, the register,
# the build log, the corrections and the audit scopes are HOW WE WORK, not
# what the software is. Several are controller-only under the working rules
# and are edited while a session is running in this same tree, which is a
# second, independent reason they are not in the index.
docs/ROUND-*.md
docs/HANDOFF-*.md
docs/HOLD-*.md
docs/scope-*.md
docs/report-*.md
docs/brief-*
docs/OPEN-ROWS-TRIAGE-*.md
docs/reports/
docs/commit-messages/
docs/midnight/
docs/round-index.md

docs/BOARD.md
docs/BUILD-ORDER.md
