# as the .md above, so the two cannot drift. Controller-only, exactly like its
# source, and it ships for the same reason that one does not: it is the plan and
# the plan is not the product.
docs/BUILD-ORDER.html
docs/NEXT.md
docs/THE-MIGRATION.md
docs/accepted-risks.md
docs/build-log.md
docs/cleanup-before-github.md
docs/corrections.md
docs/how-money-can-be-lost.md
docs/scopes.md
docs/the-doc-set.md
docs/questions-for-midnight.md

# WHERE WE DIFFER FROM THE FOUNDATION'S CODE. Publishing a list of suspected
# defects in somebody else's audited code, from our own repository, is not the
# same act as reporting them to the people who wrote it. The document exists
# so those reports can be made accurately; where they are made is a separate
# choice, and this line can be overturned.
docs/foundation-divergences.md

# Design and research material that describes decisions still being taken, a
# contract that has not been written, or a working input rather than software.
docs/account-contract-extension.md
docs/accounts-and-identity.md
docs/browser-proving-findings.md
docs/command-index.md
docs/command-order.md
docs/company-accounts.md
docs/contract-stack-briefing.md
docs/converter*.md
docs/foundation-threaded-wasm-request.md
docs/how-we-run-things.md
docs/stagenet.md
docs/the-burn-detector.md
docs/the-deploy-problem.md
docs/vaults.md


# ── THE SEVEN DOCUMENTS THAT SHIPPED AND SHOULD NOT HAVE ───────────────────
# THESE TWO RULES, AND THE THREE ABOVE, ARE THE FIVE RULES IN THIS FILE THAT
# NAME A FILE ALREADY IN THE INDEX — TEN FILES BETWEEN THEM — AND IGNORING A
# TRACKED FILE DOES NOTHING.
# UNTRACK-SHIPPED-BY-MISTAKE.command names all ten, removes them from the index
# and leaves every one of them on disk. Every other rule here is honoured from
# the first commit because the fresh `init` was built from the take list.
#
# docs/design/edges.json is 199 KB of machine JSON, already ruled stage 2. It
# is an INPUT TO A GATE rather than a document, and it records
# `clientFilesScanned`, a count of internal files.
#
# docs/handoff/ is six documents written for an internal successor — "You are
# picking up a system that moves other people's salaries" — that CITE
# DOCUMENTS WHICH DO NOT SHIP: docs/midnight/, docs/scope-identity.md,
# BACKLOG.md. A reader following them reaches nothing. identity-brief.md
# describes the OTHER repository and shipped by default.
#
# BOTH ARE KEPT ON DISK BECAUSE BOTH ARE USED HERE: edges.json is read by the
# documentation freshness gate, and docs/handoff/ is the map a person reads.
docs/design/edges.json
docs/handoff/


# ── THE AGENT DEFINITIONS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `.claude/agents/*.md` describe HOW work is checked here rather than WHAT the
# software does — the same class as CLAUDE.md above and the same reason.
# Ruled 5 Sep: not in v1, decided later. Adding a file after publication is
# easy; removing one is impossible.
.claude/


# ── LOCAL TOOLING, KEPT ON DISK AND NOT PUBLISHED ──────────────────────────
src/testing/no-attribution.test.ts

# Local maintainer tooling. Each one reads or contains a word list that is
# configuration for this working copy and not part of the published project,
# and a checker whose data is the thing it screens for publishes that data in
# the act of screening it. They are kept on disk and are not part of the
# distributed source.
scripts/check-commit-message.sh
scripts/ship-lock.sh
scripts/check-branch-name.sh
scripts/check-commit-subject.sh

# The last two were tracked before they were listed here, and ignoring a file
# that is already tracked does nothing at all — it stays in the repository and
# it stays published. They are removed from the index in the same commit that
# carries this line, and they remain on disk, unchanged, where they are used.
# The same is true of the local test listed above them.
scripts/check-shipping-language.sh
scripts/check-shipping-language.baseline
